theorem two-bounds-below-added
  note        A plain step adds its lines as they stand: x ≥ 4 and x ≥ 0
              add to x + x ≥ 4 + 0, which is the claim. Both lines are
              bounds below on x, which no pairing of a bound above with one
              below finds.
  let x ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  assume x ≥ 4                                                        (H2)
  assume x ≥ 0                                                        (H3)
  then x + x ≥ 4

1.  x + x ≥ 4
    inequalities, from H2, H3
